(6855556, 1031287, 122678, '<td valign="top">I love this shot, I was sure only a New Yorker could capture the moment. Good for you! Congratulations!!! It was my 10 and my favorite.</td>', 'I love this shot, I was sure only a New Yorker could capture the moment. Good for you! Congratulations!!! It was my 10 and my favorite.', '2012-09-03 17:33:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6855557, 1031287, 122678, '<td valign="top">Oh, yes and perfectly processed.</td>', 'Oh, yes and perfectly processed.', '2012-09-03 17:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6855558, 1031197, 122678, '<td valign="top">Great action shot. I gave it a 10. Congratulations!</td>', 'Great action shot. I gave it a 10. Congratulations!', '2012-09-03 17:35:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6855559, 1031086, 101702, '<td valign="top">Another classic... Great lighting/processing really engages the viewer in all the right places.</td>', 'Another classic... Great lighting/processing really engages the viewer in all the right places.', '2012-09-03 17:35:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6855567, 1031063, 29011, '<td valign="top">I like this one very much. I think the title applies to both subjects.  As a certified beach bum 8) I find myself with that look on myself tons of times. Checking the water out, no floating garbage, no sharks, no jellyfish, check!<br/> <br/>ETA: My only guess to the sub score, people didn''t think it was street because of the beach location? a technicality as many public(or private) beaches in the cities just barely border the street(boardwalk). Others will say any public space works. In the context of this challenge , most people want a bit of concrete in the shot to make it count as street. I guess it''s one of those things that can be discussed for ages.<br/> <br/>Still... <a href="//streetreverbmagazine.com/features/articles/the-dolphin-effect-australian-street-photography-and-the-beach" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//streetreverbmagazine.com/features/articles/the-dolphin-effect-australian-street-photography-and-the-beach</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-09-03 19:30:45.</i></td>', 'I like this one very much. I think the title applies to both subjects.  As a certified beach bum 8) I find myself with that look on myself tons of times. Checking the water out, no floating garbage, no sharks, no jellyfish, check! ETA: My only guess to the sub score, people didn''t think it was street because of the beach location? a technicality as many public(or private) beaches in the cities just barely border the street(boardwalk). Others will say any public space works. In the context of this challenge , most people want a bit of concrete in the shot to make it count as street. I guess it''s one of those things that can be discussed for ages. Still... //streetreverbmagazine.com/features/articles/the-dolphin-effect-australian-street-photography-and-the-beach', '2012-09-03 17:54:50.000000', '2012-09-03 20:30:45.000000', 0),
(6855569, 1031291, 29011, '<td valign="top">Captures the energy and vibe of the street really well. Great location too. Top20 Congrats! :)</td>', 'Captures the energy and vibe of the street really well. Great location too. Top20 Congrats! :)', '2012-09-03 17:56:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6855573, 1030674, 29011, '<td valign="top">This one really stood out for me. Made my top10 too. Probably one of my favorite uses of selective desaturtion I''ve seen in a very long time. Congrats on the top5! <br/></td>', 'This one really stood out for me. Made my top10 too. Probably one of my favorite uses of selective desaturtion I''ve seen in a very long time. Congrats on the top5! ', '2012-09-03 18:01:57.000000', NULL, 0);
